 "notes": "Curve extracted from the vector paths of Figure 14 (ALPs.eps in the arXiv e-print, Mathematica EPS): red solid 'Ellipticity PVLAS 2015' curve, the 95% c.l. model-independent laboratory exclusion from the vacuum-magnetic-birefringence (ellipticity) runs #2 and #3 (Table III). Axis calibration from the log-decade gridlines (x: 1e-4/1e-3/1e-2 eV at 83.41/184.445/285.48 pt; y: 1e-5 at 12.96 pt, 52.622 pt per decade), verified against tick labels. The paper defines L = g_a phi E.B, identical to the canonical -(g_agamma/4) a F Fdual, so g is already g_agamma in GeV^-1. The paper also shows a 'Rotation PVLAS 2015' (dichroism) curve which is slightly stronger below ~1 meV (flat at ~7.3e-8 GeV^-1 down to 1e-4 eV); the ellipticity curve reported here is the experiment's headline birefringence result and dominates for m >= 1 meV. Laboratory limit: no dark-matter density assumption, no rescaling applied.",
